1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
The names of those who had passed the Royal Knights selection exam were finally announced.

5
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Zora, who'd also passed, was late to the ceremony.

6
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:47,000
With the inclusion of three additional members, Shiren Tiam, Cobb Portaport, and Nozel Silva, Captain of the Silver Eagles,

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
the ranks of the Royal Knights would now boast a total of 20 elite warriors.

8
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Victory is all we need! The Eye of the Midnight Sun is a contemptible terrorist organization!

9
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:03,000
If we don't pull it up by the roots ourselves, our nation will never know peace!

10
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Rest assured we will be making our way to their base immediately!

11
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Listen up! It lies in the floating dungeon found within the strong magic region called Gravitostones!

12
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:24,000
!

13
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,000
!

14
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:32,740
It taks what it's like

15
00:01:32,740 --> 00:01:37,280
But Anton Schmidt

16
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:40,360
Why don't you say he's in real character?

17
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:46,780
What is it?

18
00:01:46,780 --> 00:01:52,500
But let's pretend to die

19
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:54,960
It has been there

20
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:56,000
I delle so much

21
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Action.

22
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:31,140
Oh no, we all have legal skills.

23
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:42,480
You may each see a very dark style such as time to and then pass it over.

24
00:02:42,480 --> 00:03:12,460
To be continued...

25
00:03:12,480 --> 00:03:14,400
So, um...

26
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:15,860
How's Foygolion doing?

27
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:17,940
He's still unconscious.

28
00:03:18,620 --> 00:03:21,120
After the capital was attacked, he was abducted.

29
00:03:21,860 --> 00:03:24,840
They must have done something to him, but we never figured out what it was.

30
00:03:26,180 --> 00:03:27,720
Whatever it is, it's bad.

31
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:33,020
Though, if he were conscious, I know exactly how he'd react.

32
00:03:33,860 --> 00:03:38,200
He'd say, I failed to overpower my opponent because I'm lacking experience.

33
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:43,000
Either way, it's not the end for me.

34
00:03:43,440 --> 00:03:45,620
I'll train harder and surpass you both.

35
00:03:45,920 --> 00:03:46,500
Watch me!

36
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:47,940
Wow, Leopold.

37
00:03:48,340 --> 00:03:50,360
I'll get revenge for Captain Foygolion.

38
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:51,780
Don't worry about that.

39
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:57,140
Unlike most people, he didn't laugh at my dream of becoming the next Wizard King.

40
00:03:57,480 --> 00:03:59,200
He even called me a rival.

41
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:04,440
I am who I am now, because Captain Foygolion believed in me.

42
00:04:05,180 --> 00:04:06,200
And so am I.

43
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:08,920
There isn't any shame in being weak, girl.

44
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:11,280
The shame is in staying weak.

45
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:16,000
What he said helped me to grow stronger.

46
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:19,800
Asta!

47
00:04:20,140 --> 00:04:20,540
Noelle!

48
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:21,800
I'm counting on you.

49
00:04:22,340 --> 00:04:22,900
Trust me.

50
00:04:22,960 --> 00:04:24,800
We're gonna bring peace to the Clover Kingdom.

51
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:27,400
By stopping the Eye of the Midnight Sun.

52
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:35,080
We gotta fight together soon, too, Leo.

53
00:04:35,340 --> 00:04:36,240
You're on, pal.

54
00:04:36,580 --> 00:04:37,380
Careful, Alfin.

55
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:37,940
Right.

56
00:04:38,140 --> 00:04:38,940
We'll be back.

57
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:49,780
So Captain Foygolion and Finral are both unconscious now.

58
00:04:50,020 --> 00:04:51,980
I hope they wake up before too much longer.

59
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:59,340
Actually, the way that Mana felt before, it might have had something to do with the Eye of the Midnight Sun.

60
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:03,000
We've got to defeat them fast.

61
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:03,980
You're right.

62
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:08,600
But you know, there's something that's been bugging me for a long time now.

63
00:05:10,320 --> 00:05:15,120
Well, back when I was fighting that big hairy guy, he said they'd never forgive us.

64
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:17,640
That we're fighting because we have a grudge.

65
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:23,720
So, does that mean if we forgave each other, we wouldn't have to fight?

66
00:05:24,620 --> 00:05:25,760
But who is we?

67
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:29,680
I don't know!

68
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:32,720
It feels like the more I talk about this, the more I confuse myself!

69
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:35,080
That's because you're an idiot who's trying to be deep.

70
00:05:35,220 --> 00:05:36,400
I'm not an idiot!

71
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:40,160
I ain't come to think of it, Captain Yami said the exact same thing!

72
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:42,560
Okay, I'll clear my head with some strength training!

73
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:43,900
Crunches!

74
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:47,540
And I gotta do a few back extensions, too!

75
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:49,020
You stupid brute.

76
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:52,540
So many crabs!

77
00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:54,220
Unbelievable.

78
00:05:55,700 --> 00:05:56,380
Oh, look!

79
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:58,240
You know, Mimosa and Specs are here.

80
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:01,700
Did all of you come here to visit Captain Foygolion, too?

81
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:03,800
No, I'm afraid not.

82
00:06:04,220 --> 00:06:05,760
You see, among all the magic nightroids...

83
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:06,300
Asta! Are you all right?

84
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:07,520
The golden dawn...

85
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:09,560
Yep, don't worry about me.

86
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:12,760
I've trained every last muscle in my body, so I'd be ready for anything.

87
00:06:13,100 --> 00:06:15,360
Well, you obviously forgot the strength in your brain.

88
00:06:15,760 --> 00:06:16,560
Yeah, you're right.

89
00:06:16,620 --> 00:06:18,440
My brain's still pretty weak and flabby.

90
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:19,000
Hey!

91
00:06:19,140 --> 00:06:20,040
That's not fair!

92
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:24,780
If there's a spell that makes a person smarter, can somebody cast it on Asta?

93
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:26,600
You're so thoughtful, you know!

94
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:28,700
Don't ask people to do stuff for me!

95
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:32,060
I'm sorry. I don't know one.

96
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:33,880
Oh, that's too bad.

97
00:06:34,240 --> 00:06:35,140
Back to business.

98
00:06:35,740 --> 00:06:38,940
The decisive battle is at hand, but you don't seem nervous at all.

99
00:06:39,740 --> 00:06:42,340
What do we do if an enemy spy happens to find us out?

100
00:06:42,340 --> 00:06:44,140
A spy, huh?

101
00:06:48,220 --> 00:06:50,700
It's certainly a possibility, after all.

102
00:06:51,060 --> 00:06:56,260
Think of the individuals who bribed the captain of the Purple Orcas and opened up the royal capital to attack.

103
00:06:56,960 --> 00:06:59,360
No amount of caution would be unwarranted.

104
00:07:00,140 --> 00:07:01,180
I guess not.

105
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:02,740
We'll be on guard.

106
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:08,900
Anyway, if all of us are headed into the capital, want a lift?

107
00:07:08,900 --> 00:07:10,340
We'll take my vessel.

108
00:07:12,420 --> 00:07:14,580
Are you sure you don't mind?

109
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:16,920
If you insist.

110
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:22,420
Yummy!

111
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:29,540
The food really is way better in the capital, huh?

112
00:07:31,140 --> 00:07:31,660
Oops.

113
00:07:32,340 --> 00:07:33,220
You silly.

114
00:07:33,460 --> 00:07:35,120
There's some sauce on your face.

115
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:37,220
I'm so sorry.

116
00:07:37,320 --> 00:07:38,800
That was far too presumptuous.

117
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:39,580
It's cool.

118
00:07:40,020 --> 00:07:40,700
Thanks a lot.

119
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:42,040
Don't stuff your face.

120
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:44,160
You're supposed to be on alert, remember?

121
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:47,780
And you're definitely not supposed to be getting your face wiped by a...

122
00:07:47,780 --> 00:07:48,980
I mean, not like I care.

123
00:07:49,100 --> 00:07:51,000
Do whatever you want, stupid dorksta.

124
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:53,660
Look, I promise you guys, I'm totally on the ball.

125
00:07:53,820 --> 00:07:54,700
I'm not pigging out.

126
00:07:54,740 --> 00:07:56,280
I normally ain't twice this much.

127
00:07:59,240 --> 00:07:59,720
Unbelievable.

128
00:08:00,580 --> 00:08:01,580
I'm concerned.

129
00:08:01,580 --> 00:08:04,300
It's not just Asta.

130
00:08:04,300 --> 00:08:08,940
They may be talented, but some of the royal knights have... issues.

131
00:08:10,460 --> 00:08:12,600
I can't wait to start fighting.

132
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:15,580
I'll pulverize those midnight sun guys till they're black and blue.

133
00:08:15,580 --> 00:08:20,760
Zora's all by himself.

134
00:08:21,260 --> 00:08:24,100
He's probably too shy to strike up a conversation.

135
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:26,940
Maybe I can bring him out of his shell.

136
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,300
Look what I can do.

137
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:32,260
Hey, I'm Zora Ideale.

138
00:08:32,260 --> 00:08:41,500
Oh, no, Captain Rue.

139
00:08:46,640 --> 00:08:49,000
Do none of you worms have any manners?

140
00:08:52,060 --> 00:08:57,880
When you're eating a meal, you're supposed to enjoy it in the most graceful and beautiful fashion you possibly can.

141
00:08:57,880 --> 00:09:08,700
Running away from my fork because you do not desire for me to consume you?

142
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:11,400
What a decidedly un-beautiful thing you are.

143
00:09:16,660 --> 00:09:19,140
That's my brethren, you monster!

144
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:26,800
Ladies and gentlemen, it seems Pooley would like to entertain us with an original song.

145
00:09:27,880 --> 00:09:57,200
I hate to be rude, but I'm filled with the urge to kill someone.

146
00:09:57,200 --> 00:10:04,200
I'll never get any valuable intel as long as I'm stuck to him.

147
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:18,200
Nozel, what is it you'd like to discuss with me?

148
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:23,200
The fact that we're taking three days to set our plan into motion, isn't that too cautious?

149
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:29,200
What are you implying? Do you think I'm some kind of paranoid coward?

150
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:33,200
No. It appears that my reservations were unfounded.

151
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:36,200
Huh. Somebody's a fast learner.

152
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:42,200
I've set a trap to find out the extent to which the enemy knows our movements. Everything's under control.

153
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:46,200
Now then, I have a question too.

154
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:50,200
Did you really believe you could deceive me with such an insipid spell?

155
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:59,200
Oh, Dermot!

156
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:06,200
End of the line, Spy.

157
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:16,200
He's from the Eye of the Midnight Sun?

158
00:11:16,200 --> 00:11:18,200
Wow. So they did have spies.

159
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:20,200
What a rotten trick!

160
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:25,200
Hey you, newbie. Apparently he chose you to be his conduit so he could tail us on our mission.

161
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:30,200
I can't believe I never noticed there was something amiss. What an absolute disgrace.

162
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:38,200
I've questioned this rodent within an inch of his life, and I've concluded that the enemy is not yet aware of our activities.

163
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:45,200
Therefore, I have moved up the date of departure, which means we storm their hideout first thing in the morning!

164
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:47,200
Wait! So soon?

165
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:49,200
But I thought we had three days!

166
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:53,200
No way! I don't want to let Yuno see what I look like as soon as I wake up!

167
00:11:53,200 --> 00:12:00,200
I want everyone to be at their best, so get plenty of rest tonight. That is all.

168
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:12,200
If you ask me, it seems like Captain Mary Leona must have been planning from the very beginning for us to leave immediately if she caught an enemy sneaking around.

169
00:12:12,200 --> 00:12:17,200
Well, they do say that to fool your enemies, sometimes you must begin by fooling your friends.

170
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:20,200
But still, we head out in the morning?

171
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:25,200
That Captain's really something else.

172
00:12:28,200 --> 00:12:32,200
What's got you so upset, little fella? Are you starting to get scared?

173
00:12:34,200 --> 00:12:42,200
It's the opposite. I want to become the Wizard King, so that I can bring peace and freedom to the Clover Kingdom.

174
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:45,200
I want everybody to smile.

175
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:49,200
They can't wreck our country. I won't let them!

176
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:52,200
Make sure you don't wreck our country by messing things up.

177
00:12:53,200 --> 00:12:55,200
You won't get the best of me either, Yuno!

178
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:57,200
I'm going to win.

179
00:12:58,200 --> 00:12:59,200
Well, here we go.

180
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:01,200
Right!

181
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:05,200
Tomorrow's the day. We'll finally put an end to all this.

182
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:07,200
The Royal Knights...

183
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:09,200
...will defeat the Eye of the Midnight Sun!

184
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:13,200
We'll be here for you.

185
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:14,200
Fire!

186
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:20,200
Fire!

187
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:22,200
Fire!

188
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:23,200
Fire!

189
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:23,240
Fire!

190
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:28,200
Fire!

191
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:29,200
Fire!

192
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:30,200
Fire!

193
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:31,200
Fire!

194
00:13:31,200 --> 00:13:32,200
Fire!

195
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:33,200
Fire!

196
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:36,200
Fire!

197
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:37,200
Fire!

198
00:13:37,200 --> 00:13:38,200
Fire!

199
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:40,200
Fire!

200
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:42,240
We're at the Eye of the Midnight Sun's hideout.

201
00:13:44,860 --> 00:13:49,760
There are few people who would venture into a strong magic area like this in the first place.

202
00:13:50,960 --> 00:13:53,960
And with the added obscurity from that magical mist,

203
00:13:54,160 --> 00:13:57,320
even those brave enough to seek it would have a hard time finding it.

204
00:13:57,660 --> 00:14:01,240
Let me guess, that line of thinking was what helped you pinpoint the location,

205
00:14:01,420 --> 00:14:03,280
wasn't it, Captain of the Silver Eagles?

206
00:14:04,120 --> 00:14:05,720
I must say, I'm impressed.

207
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:08,480
The discovery was nothing but a stroke of luck, I'm afraid.

208
00:14:08,480 --> 00:14:12,180
I was investigating a dungeon when I discovered the location of their hideout.

209
00:14:12,660 --> 00:14:16,740
Really? And would you care to tell me your reasoning for coming out here with us?

210
00:14:17,660 --> 00:14:17,940
Hmm?

211
00:14:18,820 --> 00:14:20,720
There's hardly time for chit-chat.

212
00:14:21,300 --> 00:14:23,780
Shirin, I believe your usual spell will work from here.

213
00:14:24,540 --> 00:14:25,140
Of course.

214
00:14:38,480 --> 00:14:43,220
Stone creation magic. Stone model of the world materialized.

215
00:14:43,400 --> 00:14:43,940
Awesome!

216
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:49,360
Yes, I see. This place is structured like an anthill that we can enter from any angle.

217
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:51,420
It should be fairly easy to invade.

218
00:14:52,900 --> 00:14:56,480
There are mages wielding senior level magic powers scattered throughout.

219
00:14:56,940 --> 00:15:00,060
And someone more powerful in the larger center space.

220
00:15:00,060 --> 00:15:02,280
I would assume that's their leader.

221
00:15:03,720 --> 00:15:06,160
Yeah, that's licked. No doubt about it.

222
00:15:06,940 --> 00:15:10,000
Nozel, sir, what is our battle strategy going to be?

223
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:13,220
I'm the captain of the Silver Eagles, not the Royal Knights.

224
00:15:13,760 --> 00:15:15,360
That's a question for Mariliona.

225
00:15:16,160 --> 00:15:17,480
Oh, right. I'm sorry.

226
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:19,120
Listen carefully!

227
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:23,240
The best way to beat them is to cause confusion with a surprise attack.

228
00:15:23,240 --> 00:15:27,780
Usually, we'd enter separately to keep them from anticipating our moves.

229
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:34,740
But, having so many points of entry means the opponent is likely to be confident in their defenses.

230
00:15:35,300 --> 00:15:39,740
The more spread out we are, the easier it will be for them to overpower us instead.

231
00:15:40,120 --> 00:15:42,960
Which means, the most logical tactic is...

232
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:43,420
I know!

233
00:15:43,800 --> 00:15:47,280
We just have to psych ourselves up so we can fight these guys even harder!

234
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:51,300
I can take care of them myself. No psyching up necessary.

235
00:15:51,300 --> 00:15:54,200
I'll beat them senseless and crush their bones into powder!

236
00:15:55,100 --> 00:15:58,880
I shall use my immaculate power to clear them out in one beautiful swoop!

237
00:15:59,260 --> 00:16:00,680
Please just disappear.

238
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:02,720
I'm surrounded by morons.

239
00:16:03,260 --> 00:16:04,440
Balance is key.

240
00:16:05,740 --> 00:16:09,540
If the idea is to break up their numbers and still be able to overcome them,

241
00:16:09,700 --> 00:16:12,220
then the best plan is to split into teams of four.

242
00:16:12,860 --> 00:16:14,060
Don't you agree, Captain?

243
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:15,400
Wholeheartedly!

244
00:16:16,460 --> 00:16:19,420
So we'll divide into five teams of four and make our move!

245
00:16:19,420 --> 00:16:23,800
As long as I'm not stuck on the same team as this obnoxious Rugrat, I guess I'll be alright with anything.

246
00:16:24,340 --> 00:16:27,260
Look, just because your mask is cool doesn't mean you get to be rude!

247
00:16:27,420 --> 00:16:29,380
Plus, you're the obnoxious one around here!

248
00:16:30,380 --> 00:16:30,740
Oh.

249
00:16:31,280 --> 00:16:34,200
Then again, I don't think anybody's gonna want to work with you anyway,

250
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:37,060
so I guess I'll be a nice person and let you be a part of my team.

251
00:16:37,460 --> 00:16:40,480
You'll change your tune when I save your weak ass from certain death.

252
00:16:40,480 --> 00:16:45,400
You problem children are on my team. Behave yourselves.

253
